{"id":"kerioth","name":"Kerioth","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:kerioth"],"groups":["2. Also called KIRIOTH"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Kerioth","text":"Cities. (1.) A town in the south of Judah (Josh. 15:25). Judas the traitor was probably a native of this place, and hence his name Iscariot. It has been identified with the ruins of el-Kureitein, about 10 miles south of Hebron. (See HAZOR [4]). (2.) A city of Moab (Jer. 48:24, 41), called Kirioth (Amos 2:2)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7152","lemma":"קְרִיּוֹת","xlit":"Qᵉrîyôwth","gloss":"Kerioth, the name of two places in Palestine","kjv":"Kerioth, Kirioth","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","xlit":"Môwʼâb","gloss":"Moab, an incestuous son of Lot","kjv":"Moab","count":3,"share":0.75}],"verses":["Josh.15.25","Jer.48.24","Jer.48.41","Amos.2.2"],"related":[{"id":"ammonites","type":"lexical","strong":"H4124","why":"both lead with מוֹאָב (H4124)"},{"id":"ar","type":"lexical","strong":"H4124","why":"both lead with מוֹאָב (H4124)"},{"id":"chemosh","type":"lexical","strong":"H4124","why":"both lead with מוֹאָב (H4124)"},{"id":"kir-haraseth","type":"lexical","strong":"H4124","why":"both lead with מוֹאָב (H4124)"},{"id":"kirjathaim","type":"lexical","strong":"H4124","why":"both lead with מוֹאָב (H4124)"},{"id":"mesha","type":"lexical","strong":"H4124","why":"both lead with מוֹאָב (H4124)"}],"works":[]}
